course: dictionary
lesson: 5831
title: Mainly and mostly
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Mainly means mostly, or more than anything else. When you meet it, ask yourself: what is the biggest part? «Air is mainly nitrogen» tells you nitrogen is the largest part of air, not the only part.
explain: Read the words around it for clues. «The diet is mainly plants» means plants make up most of the food, and other foods are there too. Swap in mostly: «The diet is mostly plants» still makes sense, so you have the right meaning.
explain: Mainly often comes before a reason, as in «mainly because». «Young children get stronger mainly because the brain learns to switch on more fibres at once.» The word tells you the main reason out of several possible ones.
fact: Mainly means mostly, more than anything else, or in most cases.
fact: Similar words include «mostly», «largely» and «chiefly».
fact: «Hospitals are mainly places of help and healing» means most of what hospitals do is help people.
fact: «Spots come mainly from hormones, skin and genes» names the main causes, not every cause.
fact: Mainly is an adverb, so it tells us how much or to what extent something is true.
exercise: «Air is mainly nitrogen.» What does mainly mean here? | Only, with nothing else at all | *Mostly, as the biggest part | Quickly | Never
exercise: In «hospitals are mainly places of help and healing», which word could replace mainly? | Rarely | *Mostly | Angrily | Suddenly
exercise: «Spots come mainly from hormones, skin and genes; one chocolate bar will not cause a breakout.» What does this tell you about chocolate? | It is the only cause of spots | It cures spots | *It is not the main cause of spots | It is the main cause of spots
test: «English spread from one small island to more than 50 countries mainly through trade, settlement and empire.» What were the main ways English spread? | Television only | Sunshine and rain | *Trade, settlement and empire | Football matches
test: Which sentence uses mainly correctly? | The class mainly walked the school. | *Most of the class walked to school, mainly because it was sunny. | Mainly the sun is school.
exam: Which is the best meaning of mainly? | Only | Never | Very quickly | *Mostly, more than anything else
